{{Documentation}}
As a note, please do not take any examples on this page as factual information about game content as they are solely for the purpose of demonstrating the usage of this template.

==Basic Usage==
This template is a profile template that is used for generating a tierlist. Its basic usage is simple and intuitive, only needing to state tier names and items in the tierlist with additional settings to make the tierlist more elaborate. For each tier, an argument containing " Tier" is passed such that the following items are included in that tier. Below is an example of a basic tierlist for Cats:

<tabber>
Source=
<pre>
{{Tierlist
|S Tier
|Cat|Tank Cat
|A Tier
|King Dragon Cat
|B Tier
|Axe Cat|Lion Cat|Mythical Titan Cat
}}
</pre>

|-|Result=
{{Tierlist
|S Tier
|Cat|Tank Cat
|A Tier
|King Dragon Cat
|B Tier
|Axe Cat|Lion Cat|Mythical Titan Cat
}}
</tabber>

==Modes==
The template has five different modes to deal with different items in the tierlist. They are <code>cat</code>, <code>enemy</code>, <code>image</code>, <code>text</code>, and <code>user</code>. The first was explained in the section above, requiring accurate Cat names to be typed as arguments. Similarly, the <code>enemy</code> mode takes enemy names and displays enemy icons. The other two modes, <code>image</code> and <code>text</code> directly include the inputs in the tierlist as wikitext. The difference between the two is that the former uses space as a separator and the latter uses a comma and a space as a separator. This is because each separator makes more sense with each usage (you wouldn't want to see commas with images). The final mode, <code>user</code>, takes usernames. The tabs below show examples for each mode.

