==Parameters==
Many parameters exist to make the tierlist customizable. Below are explanations of each:
*<code>title</code> puts a title row on the top of the tierlist, the argument is directly used as the title.
*<code>mode</code> specifies the mode for the tierlist, explained in the points below.
**<code>mode = cat</code> displays icons for each cat specified by exact name. Differentiates forms.
**<code>mode = enemy</code> displays enemy icons for each enemy specified by exact name.
**<code>mode = image</code> displays images with regular wikitext separated by spaces.
**<code>mode = text</code> displays wikitext separated by commas.
**<code>mode = user</code> displays profile images and linked usernames.
*<code>color</code> sets the color of the column for tier names.
**<code>color = custom</code> allows any colors to be used from top to bottom in hex codes, if not enough colors are not supplied for all rows, default heading cell color is used for remaining rows.
**<code>color = linear</code> puts a linear gradient between the two supplied colors (in hexadecimal) starting from the topmost row to the bottommost row.
**<code>color = rainbow</code> automatically applies a gradient that makes the rows be in a rainbow with red at the top and magenta at the bottom.
*<code>notier</code> removes the text " Tier" that is put in the heading cells for each tier. Inserting any text works, but it can't be empty. This parameter makes it possible to name the tiers to any text that doesn't include " Tier".
*<code>normaltier</code> Disables the formatting done on tier names and makes them normal text when tiers have colors.
*<code>size</code> scales images by the given factor in modes <code>cat</code> and <code>enemy</code>.
*<code>separator</code> sets a custom separator for items in the tierlist in case something other than " " or ", " is wanted.
*<code>textcolor</code> sets text color as some form of color that can be used in raw CSS (hexadecimal codes work).
*<code>background</code> sets the color for the background of the right column for the items.
*<code>titlecss</code> allows raw css for the title cell to be inserted.
*<code>tablecss</code> allows raw css for the entire tierlist to be inserted.

